### 2. Critical Track Section Analysis (distFromStart 3200 m – 3300 m)                                                  
                                                                                                                        
The ONE section of the track that costs the most time and comes closest to damage is Turn 11 (the final hairpin before  
the start/finish straight) in the range distFromStart 3200.0 m – 3300.0 m (specifically corner entry at ~3210 m, apex at
~3285.8 m, exit at ~3290.0 m).                                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
#### Observations (Direct Telemetry Measurements)                                                                       
                                                                                                                        
- Lowest Corner Speed: Speed dropped to 62.4 km/h at step 4912 (distFromStart = 3285.5 m), which is the absolute minimum
  cornering speed on the entire moving lap.                                                                             
- Highest Track Displacement: |trackPos| reached 0.802 (at step 4920, distFromStart = 3288.2 m, trackPos = -0.802). This
  is the only section on the entire track where |trackPos| exceeded TRACK_MARGIN (0.70) and engaged                     
  EXTRA_CENTERING_GAIN.                                                                                                 
- Minimum Forward Clearance: track9 (0° ray) dropped to 6.7 m at step 4907 (distFromStart = 3283.9 m), the lowest       
  forward distance logged anywhere on the track.                                                                        
- Steering Saturation: Steering was locked at full saturation (steer = +1.00) for 67 consecutive ticks (steps 4857–4923,
  duration 1.34 s, distFromStart 3266.0 m – 3289.4 m).                                                                  
- Time Cost: The car spent 3.94 s (197 ticks) traversing the 100 m sector from 3200 m to 3300 m, tying with the standing
  start sector (0–100 m) as the slowest 100 m interval of the lap.                                                      
- Comparison with the Previous Crash Hairpin (2400–2550 m): The hairpin at ~2468 m was negotiated cleanly with a minimum
  speed of 72.5 km/h, max |trackPos| of -0.524, minimum track9 of 14.3 m, and 0 damage.                                 
                                                                                                                        
#### Hypotheses (Inferred Mechanics)                                                                                    
                                                                                                                        
- Proximity to Damage: The car came within ~1.2 m of the outer barrier (trackPos = -0.802) under full steering lock     
  (steer = 1.00), indicating significant understeer at corner exit. Entering at ~128.8 km/h at 3200 m with conservative 
  braking onset kept the vehicle slightly fast relative to the corner radius before the apex.                           
- Time Loss: Because V_CORNER_MIN = 55.0 km/h and side rays (±30°) are heavily constrained in tight corners (openness ≈ 
  0.05), target speed was clamped low. Combined with braking deceleration, this created a protracted low-speed          
  transition spanning ~90 meters.                                                                                       
                                                                                                                        
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                                        
                                                                                                                        
### 3. Proposed Parameter Change                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
Change: Increase PARAMS["V_CORNER_BONUS"] (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:30) from 35.0 km/h to 45.0 km/h.                     
                                                                                                                        
- Formula Context:                                                                                                      
  $$\text{openness} = \text{clip}\left(\frac{\min(\text{track}[4], \text{track}[14])}{200.0}, 0, 1\right)$$             
  $$V_{\text{corner}} = V_{\text{CORNER_MIN}} + V_{\text{CORNER_BONUS}} \times \text{openness}$$                        
  $$v_{\text{target}} = \min\left(V_{\text{MAX}}, \sqrt{V_{\text{corner}}^2 + 2 \cdot \text{BRAKE_DECEL} \cdot          
  d}\right)$$                                                                                                           
- Expected Effect:                                                                                                      
    - Preserves Hairpin Safety: In tight hairpins (e.g. dist ~2468 m and ~3285 m), side sensors track[4] and track[14]  
      read only ~10–15 m, making $\text{openness} \approx 0.05\text{--}0.08$. Increasing V_CORNER_BONUS by +10 km/h     
      raises corner target speed by only +0.5 to +0.8 km/h, leaving the critical safety margin in the hairpins intact.  
    - High Gain in Open Sectors: In sweeping curves and open straights ($\text{openness} \approx 0.4\text{--}1.0$),     
      corner speed increases by +4.0 to +10.0 km/h, lifting the 200 m lookahead target speed cap from ~210.7 km/h to    
      ~215.1 km/h and allowing the car to carry significantly higher momentum through fast sectors.                     
- Risk: Low. Sweeping corners with wide geometry will be taken faster; if the car drifts wide, the existing edge        
  protection (TRACK_MARGIN = 0.70, EXTRA_CENTERING_GAIN = 1.20) automatically intervenes.                               
                                                                                                                        
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                                        
                                                                                                                        
